The internet itself grew from ARPANET, a defence-space era network — space investment catalyses technology platforms that reshape economies for decades.
Climate monitoring from orbit provides data no ground-based system can match: sea level, ice cover, deforestation, and ocean temperature are measured globally in real time.
Asteroid detection programmes (DART, Spaceguard) are the only defence against extinction-level impacts — a unique cost-benefit proposition.
International collaboration on the ISS has maintained scientific cooperation between the US and Russia even during political crises — space is a unique diplomatic channel.
